## 3. The roots lie strictly inside the intended rotation cells

For each of the twelve train angles the root box is either a point interval, for a frozen parameter, or

\[
[\alpha_e-r,\alpha_e+r].
\]

For one face with stored tuple

\[
(A_1,A_2,B_1,B_2),
\]

the five physical exterior-turn intervals are evaluated directly in radians:

\[
\begin{aligned}
G_0&=\alpha_{A_1},\\
G_1&=\alpha_{A_2}-\alpha_{A_1},\\
G_2&=\pi+\alpha_{B_1}-\alpha_{A_2},\\
G_3&=\alpha_{B_2}-\alpha_{B_1},\\
G_4&=\pi-\alpha_{B_2}.
\end{aligned}
\tag{3.1}
\]

The verifier proves on the entire certified root box

\[
0<G_i<{2\pi\over3},
\qquad
{2\pi\over3}<G_i+G_{i+1}<\pi
\tag{3.2}
\]

for every face and cyclic index. Thus no certified root sits on a wall of the rational cell.

Across all 35 certificates the weakest rigorous margins are still macroscopic relative to `r`:

\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{one-turn margin}&>0.09498,\\
\text{adjacent lower margin}&>0.04651,\\
\text{adjacent upper margin}&>0.08112
\end{aligned}
\]

in radians.

