## 4. Regularity and the two-dimensional local manifold

For a certified representative, (2.1) implies that the recorded approximate inverse is a true inverse witness for the ten-variable partial Jacobian at the exact root. In particular that `10 x 10` submatrix is nonsingular.

The full closure derivative has ten rows, so its rank is exactly ten. With twelve train-angle variables, the implicit-function theorem gives a local smooth solution manifold of dimension

\[
\boxed{12-10=2.}
\tag{4.1}
\]

This matches the two-dimensional internal tangent lower bound proved independently for every collapsed support-six block. Here, however, the statement is finite and nonlinear for 35 specific symmetry types: the infinitesimal directions integrate locally because these are regular exact closure points.

No claim is made that the same two-dimensional finite integration holds at every collapsed solution or in the seven unresolved rotation-cell orbits.

---

## 5. Symmetry transfers the representative roots to 324 labelled cells

The existing 42-orbit quotient uses only:

1. relabelings within the positive-anchor set `{0,1,2}` and within the negative-anchor set `{3,4,5}` that preserve the chosen missing matching; and
2. reflection in the common anchor line.

A sign-preserving relabeling merely permutes rows and relation-edge variables in (1.1), so it preserves exact closure and all strict turn inequalities.

Under reflection,

\[
\alpha_e\mapsto\pi-\alpha_e,
\qquad
z_e\mapsto-\overline{z_e},
\]

and the coherent relation orientation reverses. The incidence sign therefore also changes. Their product sends

\[
Bz\mapsto\overline{Bz}.
\]

Since the anchor vector `s` is real, `Bz=-s` is preserved. This is exactly the reflection action already used by the audited rotation-cell quotient.

The all-cross matching has fifteen orbits, each of size twelve. The two uncertified all-cross representatives are `0` and `2`, so the certified all-cross representatives cover

\[
13\cdot12=156
\]

of the 180 labelled cells.

The mixed matching has twenty-seven orbits. The five uncertified mixed representatives `15,18,19,22,26` each have orbit size eight. Hence the certified mixed representatives cover

\[
208-5\cdot8=168
\]

labelled cells. Altogether,

\[
\boxed{156+168=324.}
\tag{5.1}
\]

---

## 6. What the seven unresolved orbits mean

The certificate deliberately makes no claim about representatives

\[
0,2,15,18,19,22,26.
\]

Numerical constrained optimization repeatedly drives the closure residual toward zero only as one or more strict rotation-cell inequalities approach equality. That is evidence that these seven cells may be boundary-only for the nonlinear closure variety. It is not a proof. No numerical optimization result is used in the exact 35-orbit theorem.

A useful future target is therefore sharply finite: derive an analytic or exact semialgebraic obstruction for these seven representatives. If they are indeed empty, the 42-orbit nonlinear-closure classification would be complete: exactly 35 orbits would be locally feasible.

But even that classification would not close support six. The audited seven-crossing theorem is global and already shows that any actual collapsed block must realize at least seven internal train crossings with the forced crossing rotations. The 35 certified local manifolds do not supply those global stopped-train embeddings.

---

## 7. Consequence for the proof strategy

Before this certificate, one plausible route was that imposing exact six-pentagon closure on the 42 rational rotation cells might remove most of the collapsed endpoint before difficult global train topology was needed.

That route is now sharply limited:

\[
\boxed{35/42\text{ rotation-cell orbits, covering }324/388\text{ labelled cells, contain regular exact local closure roots}.}
\]

The load-bearing obstruction must therefore be global for most cells. The current seven-crossing floor is exactly such a constraint. The most useful next work is to classify seven-or-more-crossing planarizations under the forced crossing rotations, or combine the new rhombus payment with the live terminal budgets. Spending substantial effort on local closure feasibility of the already-certified 35 orbits cannot close C-II.

**Disposition:** exact nonlinear closure is present and regular in 35 of the 42 collapsed support-six rotation-cell symmetry orbits, covering 324 of 388 labelled cells. Seven orbit representatives remain unresolved at the local closure level. C-II remains open because global stopped-train integrability and diameter locking are not certified by these local roots.
